From 9425368b693273e4062f328bc0427a6f3dcdc2cb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 00:07:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] delegation: keep a requested stop across shutdown;
 log "not woken" only for notes

Follow-up to PR #1683 review 5880847320 (non-blocking nits).

1. A /stop (interrupt_all reason='/stop', or the gateway's interrupt_for_session
   reason='stop_command') followed by a gateway shutdown before the unit's runner
   unwound let interrupt_all(by_shutdown=True) stamp the still-active unit with
   interrupted_by, so its result woke the parent on work the user chose to stop.
   _mark_stop records the first stop's intent: a requested stop marks
   _stop_requested and a later shutdown sweep no longer stamps it; a shutdown stop
   stays stamped when a requested stop follows.

2. _watch_notification_metadata warned "parent not woken" for every requested-stop
   delegation result, including viewed parents whose result then runs as a turn.
   It now only flags the admission (completion_requested_stop -> descriptor
   requested_stop, validated against the stopped statuses); note_if_unviewed logs
   the warning when the result is actually kept as a note (no viewer attached).

Tests: Event-controlled regressions for /stop and stop_command before a shutdown
sweep (plus shutdown-only and shutdown-then-stop controls), metadata validation,
and the real viewed/unviewed executor route. Red on base (12 fail); 11/11 mutants
killed; 37 related files 542 passed, 1 skipped.
